WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.618 --> 00:00:03.754
CALL.

00:00:02.653 --> 00:00:04.956
CHRIS.

00:00:03.888 --> 00:00:06.324
&gt;&gt; Chris: JONATHAN HUNT

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:07.225
REPORTING FROM LAS VEGAS.

00:00:06.457 --> 00:00:10.928
JONATHAN, THANKS FOR THAT.

00:00:07.358 --> 00:00:11.662
SENATE LEADER MITCH McCONNELL

00:00:11.062 --> 00:00:14.565
MADE HISTORY TODAY.

00:00:11.796 --> 00:00:15.333
CORRESPONDENT PETER DOOCY TELLS

00:00:14.699 --> 00:00:16.467
US HOW.

00:00:15.466 --> 00:00:17.635
&gt;&gt; MITCH McCONNELL BECAME

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:19.370
SENATE REPUBLICAN LEADER 11

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:21.706
YEARS FIVE MONTHS AND TEN DAYS

00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:23.441
AGO AND NOW HE HAS HAD THE TOP

00:00:21.839 --> 00:00:25.743
SPOT A DAY LONGER THAN FORMER

00:00:23.574 --> 00:00:26.978
SENATOR BOB DOLE MAKING HIM THE

00:00:25.876 --> 00:00:27.712
LONGEST TENURED G.O.P. LEADER

00:00:27.111 --> 00:00:29.247
EVER.

00:00:27.845 --> 00:00:31.716
&gt;&gt; HE UNDERSTANDS THE SENATE

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.717
BETTER THAN ANYBODY ELSE HERE.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:34.785
&gt;&gt; FORMER SENATOR TRENT LOT HAD

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.320
THE JOB FOR FIVE YEARS.

00:00:34.919 --> 00:00:38.522
&gt;&gt; I THINK IT WAS THE TOUGHEST

00:00:36.454 --> 00:00:39.523
WE ARE SHIPPED OUT, POLITICAL

00:00:38.656 --> 00:00:40.258
JOB IN THE CITY.

00:00:39.657 --> 00:00:42.893
&gt;&gt; McCONNELL SAYS HE PLAYS THE

00:00:40.391 --> 00:00:45.196
LONG GAME.

00:00:43.027 --> 00:00:47.365
FAILED TO REPEAL OBAMACARE.

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:48.532
IN 2010 HE TOOK IT FOR OUTLINING

00:00:47.498 --> 00:00:49.367
A DIFFERENT PRIORITY.

00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:51.769
&gt;&gt; OUR TOP POLITICAL PRIORITY

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.437
OVER THE NEXT TWO YEARS SHOULD

00:00:51.902 --> 00:00:54.338
BE TO DENY PRESIDENT OBAMA A

00:00:53.571 --> 00:01:00.111
SECOND TERM.

00:00:54.472 --> 00:01:01.112
&gt;&gt; SIX YEARS LATER WHEN OUTGOING

00:01:00.244 --> 00:01:02.179
PRESIDENT BARACK OBAMA MERRICK

00:01:01.245 --> 00:01:04.148
GARLAND TO THE COURT, HE

00:01:02.313 --> 00:01:04.882
DECLINED TO CONSIDER HIM.

00:01:04.282 --> 00:01:06.717
&gt;&gt; THE AMERICAN PEOPLE NEED TO

00:01:05.016 --> 00:01:08.919
WEIGH IN AND DECIDE WHO'S GOING

00:01:06.851 --> 00:01:10.154
TO MAKE THIS DECISION.

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:10.721
&gt;&gt; DEMOCRATS CRITICIZED HIM FOR

00:01:10.288 --> 00:01:17.128
MAKING THIS DECISION.

00:01:10.855 --> 00:01:18.129
&gt;&gt; WE ARE SETTING A DANGEROUS

00:01:17.261 --> 00:01:18.763
PRECEDENT.

00:01:18.262 --> 00:01:19.563
&gt;&gt; McCONNELL LATER HELPED

00:01:18.896 --> 00:01:20.631
CONFIRMED NEIL GORSUCH.

00:01:19.697 --> 00:01:22.767
&gt;&gt; HE IS REASONABLY ABLE TO

00:01:20.765 --> 00:01:24.535
CONTROL HIS PEOPLE.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.636
THAT IN ITSELF IS SOMETHING TO

00:01:24.669 --> 00:01:27.638
BE CREDITED WITH.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.674
&gt;&gt; HE'S ALSO THE RARE REPUBLICAN

00:01:27.772 --> 00:01:32.510
WHO DARES TO SHARE LAUGHS IN

00:01:29.807 --> 00:01:33.411
PUBLIC WITH HIS DEMOCRATIC

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.145
COUNTERPARTS.

00:01:33.544 --> 00:01:35.346
&gt;&gt; HE PLAYS HIS CARDS CLOSE TO

00:01:34.278 --> 00:01:37.348
HIS CHEST BUT HE WILL JUST SIT

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:38.115
THERE AND LISTEN AND LISTEN AND

00:01:37.481 --> 00:01:39.016
LISTEN.

00:01:38.249 --> 00:01:40.584
&gt;&gt; SOMETIMES REPUBLICANS BREAK

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.852
RANKS, LIKE SENATOR TED CRUZ WHO

00:01:40.718 --> 00:01:44.388
ONCE CALLED McCONNELL OUT

00:01:41.986 --> 00:01:45.222
ABOUT THE EXPORT-IMPORT BANK.

00:01:44.522 --> 00:01:47.858
&gt;&gt; I CANNOT BELIEVE HE WOULD

00:01:45.356 --> 00:01:48.759
TELL A FLAT OUT LIE.

00:01:47.992 --> 00:01:50.528
&gt;&gt; THERE ARE ALSO REPUBLICAN

00:01:48.893 --> 00:01:52.196
CANDIDATES WHO TRY TO CAPITALIZE

00:01:50.661 --> 00:01:55.333
ON ANTI-McCONNELL SENTIMENT.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:56.100
&gt;&gt; ONE OF MY GOALS AS U.S.

00:01:55.466 --> 00:01:57.702
SENATOR WILL BE TO DITCH COCAINE

00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:58.436
MITCH.

00:01:57.835 --> 00:02:01.339
&gt;&gt; IN D.C. THERE'S NOT MUCH OF

00:01:58.569 --> 00:02:01.939
AN APPETITE TO REMOVE THE

00:02:01.472 --> 00:02:03.574
REPUBLICAN LEADER.

00:02:02.073 --> 00:02:04.342
&gt;&gt; HE'S BEEN RIGHT SO MANY TIMES

00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:06.944
SO IT BUILDS CONFIDENCE.

00:02:04.475 --> 00:02:08.979
&gt;&gt; BUT ON THIS, THE DAY THAT

00:02:07.078 --> 00:02:10.081
McCONNELL FINALLY BROKE THE

00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:11.816
RECORD, HIS OWN MEMBERS AREN'T

00:02:10.214 --> 00:02:12.483
LISTENING TO HIM.

00:02:11.949 --> 00:02:16.187
MULTIPLE REPUBLICAN SENATORS

00:02:12.616 --> 00:02:18.089
HAVE TOLD ME THAT TODAY AT LUNCH

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.291
McCONNELL IMPLORED REPUBLICANS

00:02:18.222 --> 00:02:21.325
TO STOP BLOCKING REPUBLICAN

00:02:20.424 --> 00:02:22.727
AMENDMENTS AND MULTIPLE

00:02:21.459 --> 00:02:25.029
REPUBLICAN SENATORS PROCEEDED TO

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.964
LEAVE LUNCH AND BLOCK EACH

